# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Upstream packages that [omamobile] carries unchanged, to hold phones at a
# version our patches support. [omamobile] comes first in the phone's
# pacman.conf, so its copy wins over the newer one in [omarchy]: phones stay
# on it through `omarchy update`, and images built from out/repo install it.
#
# tools/build-packages fetches each file (once: it stays in out/repo) from the
# first of its URLs that gives the SHA-256 here, and signs it with the release
# key like our own packages. List upstream's URL first, then our published
# copy (pkgs.omamobile.org), for when upstream prunes the old version; the
# checksum makes any copy safe. A pin never takes the name of a package
# under packages/. Removing a line takes the package out of out/repo at the next
# build, and phones move on to [omarchy]'s version at their next update.
# Check a new line's file against the upstream signature before adding it
# (pacman-key --verify FILE.sig FILE).
#
# <sha256> <url> [<url of the same file>...]

# Omarchy 4.0.6: the Omarchy patch series (packages/omamobile-omarchy/patches)
# doesn't apply to 4.5, and 4.5's migrations install packages that replace
# ours (#433, #434). Unpin when omamobile-omarchy ships a series for 4.5.
# omarchy-settings is pinned with it: omarchy depends on exactly its version.
